  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Provision of Services in Relation to Global Pre-Departure Cultural Orientation for Australia&apos;s Refugee and Special Humanitarian Program Clients for 2022-2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">For almost two decades, IOM and the Government of Australia have worked in partnership in order to deliver pre-departure Australian Cultural Orientation (AUSCO) training for Australia-bound refugees and humanitarian entrants. The program is funded by the Department of Home Affairs and has been delivered by IOM since 2003.IOM Thailand is host to the AUSCO Global Office which oversees permanent AUSCO implementing and coordinating missions in Thailand, Malaysia, Indonesia, Nepal, India, Pakistan, Iraq, Turkey, Lebanon, Jordan, Egypt, Kenya and El Salvador. AUSCO has been further delivered in Sudan and Uganda, and through mobile facilitation in more 40 other countries. The program&#x2019;s objectives are several-fold and include empowering refugees and humanitarian entrants with information on life in Australia, whilst also encouraging language training on arrival, and equipping participants with the basic skills and necessary tools needed to deal with initial challenges experienced during their settlement journey and to reach self-sufficiency. Through a 5-day course, AUSCO provides the opportunity for participants to be provided with practical advice and accurate information on the departure and settlement processes, and an opportunity to ask questions about travel to and life in Australia, including pathways and access to further education and employment, learning English and understanding laws.</narrative>
  </description>
